    "author": "cureparkinsons.org.uk"
  },
  {
    "uri": "at://did:plc:n72oektx3bsygejhsk7voyti/app.bsky.feed.post/3mxkcgkwsxc2n",
    "text": "My dad brought home newspapers & jokes hed heard after work. At dinner, we’d talk about the news, listen to his jokes. Every Sunday, he took my baby sister for a walk & theyd talk about the Mets, what kind of dog we’d get if we moved. He taught my older sis how to fix her car & told me war stories.",
